<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 April, from 217 to 1973.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">217 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,809 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Caracalla is murdered near Carrhae</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracalla">Caracalla</a> was stabbed to death by a soldier while travelling to a temple near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carrhae">Carrhae</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. His praetorian prefect Macrinus, who had arranged the killing, became the first emperor not of senatorial rank.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">876 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,150 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Abbasids defeat Ya'qub ibn al-Layth at Dayr al-Aqul</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, the Abbasid regent al-Muwaffaq defeated the Saffarid ruler Ya'qub ibn al-Layth, who was marching on Baghdad, after flooding the ground before his army. Ya'qub abandoned his attempt to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzistan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dayr-al-aqul">Battle of Dayr al-Aqul</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-ibn-al-layth-al-saffar">Ya'qub ibn al-Layth al-Saffar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1093">1093 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">933 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Norman cathedral at Winchester is consecrated</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Walkelin's Romanesque cathedral at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a> was consecrated in the presence of bishops and abbots. Later extended, it is now the longest medieval cathedral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1820">1820 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Farmer unearths the Venus de Milo on Milos</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A peasant named Yorgos Kentrotas found the marble statue in the ruins of ancient Milos. Bought by the French and taken to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a>, the armless Aphrodite became one of the most famous sculptures in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1904">1904 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France sign the Entente Cordiale</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A set of agreements settled colonial disputes, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> recognised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. The understanding ended centuries of rivalry and drew the two powers together before 1914.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1913">1913 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">113 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Seventeenth Amendment introduces direct election of US senators</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>'s ratification completed the Seventeenth Amendment, transferring the choice of senators from state legislatures to voters. Secretary of State Bryan certified it at the end of May.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1953">1953 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jomo Kenyatta is convicted at the Kapenguria trial</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A colonial court in Kenya sentenced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jomo-kenyatta">Jomo Kenyatta</a> and five others to seven years' hard labour for allegedly managing Mau Mau. The widely criticised verdict made him a national symbol; he became Kenya's first president.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pablo Picasso dies at Mougins aged 91</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Pablo Picasso</a> died at his home in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Co-founder of Cubism and creator of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guernica">Guernica</a>, he had reshaped modern art over a career lasting more than seventy years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Pablo Picasso</a></div></div></li></ol>
